/-
  SkewAdjointExponential: the exponential of a skew-adjoint matrix is unitary and, when traceless,
  lands in `SU(n)` — the estate's `su(n)` exponentiates into Mathlib's `specialUnitaryGroup`, and
  the gauge group `SU(4) × SU(2)_L × SU(2)_R` is reached from the estate's own Lie algebra

  Campaign 3 hardening unit 188 (20 September 2026). Spine links L10 (gauge algebra embedding — the
  group level, gap N4), L15 (Higgs sector) and L16 (anomaly cancellation).

  WHY. L16's row says *no group*; L10's says the group level *"has no declaration and rests on the
  `Mₙ(ℂ) → SU(n)` postulate"* (`ASSUMPTIONS_LEDGER` 11); `PatiSalamOnSixteen`'s header says
  *"`SU(4)`, `SU(2)`, `Spin(10)` exist nowhere in the estate"*; `TracelessSkewDimension`'s
  `traceless` is called that and not `su` because *"nothing here says it is the tangent space of a
  smooth group"*, and `TracelessSkewLie` and `PatiSalamStabiliserLie` record that
  `Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup` is mentioned in no file. Queried before writing:
  `specialUnitaryGroup` occurs in `paper_f` in exactly those three prose lines and in no
  declaration; `unitaryGroup` over `ℂ` occurs as `Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin n) ℂ` in
  `HermitianSignatureEigenvalues.unitaryUnit` and as the Stone chain's own `FiniteStone.unitaryGroup
  H t` (the one-parameter group `e^{itH}` of a self-adjoint operator on a Hilbert space — an
  operator group, not a matrix group); the matrix exponential is used in five files (the cutoff
  chain, `SchurExponential`, `HermiteCompleteness`), never to land in a group. This file puts the
  group there, from the Lie algebra the Higgs units use.

  WHAT IS PROVED, for every `n` (including `0`).
  (1) **`exp_mem_unitaryGroup`**: `X` skew-adjoint ⟹ `exp X ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin n) ℂ`
      (`exp X · star (exp X) = exp X · exp (−X) = exp 0 = 1`, by `Matrix.exp_conjTranspose` and
      `Matrix.exp_add_of_commute`).
  (2) **`det_exp_smul_of_isHermitian`**: `H` Hermitian ⟹ `det (exp (c • H)) = exp (c · tr H)` — the
      spectral theorem (`IsHermitian.spectral_theorem`, `eigenvectorUnitary`) diagonalises,
      `Matrix.exp_conj` and `Matrix.det_conj` strip the unitary, `Matrix.exp_diagonal` and
      `det_diagonal` reduce to `∏ exp (c λᵢ) = exp (c ∑ λᵢ)`, and `trace_eq_sum_eigenvalues`
      finishes. Mathlib has no `det (exp A) = exp (tr A)` in any form (queried: `det_exp`,
      `exp_trace` absent), and neither did the estate; this is the Hermitian-direction case, which
      is all the skew-adjoint algebras need.
  (3) `isHermitian_neg_I_smul` (`X` skew-adjoint ⟹ `(−i) • X` Hermitian), hence
      **`det_exp_of_skewAdjoint`**: `det (exp X) = exp (tr X)`, and
      **`exp_mem_specialUnitaryGroup`**:
      `X` skew-adjoint and traceless ⟹ `exp X ∈ Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin n) ℂ`.
  (4) **`expSU : traceless n → specialUnitaryGroup (Fin n) ℂ`** on this estate's `su(n)`
      (`TracelessSkewDimension.traceless`, the kernel of the imaginary trace on `skewAdjoint`),
      with `expSU_val`; **`oneParam A t := expSU (t • A)`**, the one-parameter subgroup of `SU(n)`
      generated by `A ∈ su(n)`: `oneParam_zero` and **`oneParam_add`** (`exp ((s + t) • A) =
      exp (s • A) · exp (t • A)`, the two summands commuting).
  (5) **`expFull : Full → SU(4) × SU(2) × SU(2)`** — unit 183's `Full = traceless 4 × traceless 2 ×
      traceless 2` exponentiated factor by factor: the Pati–Salam gauge GROUP as a type inhabited
      from the Lie algebra the Higgs units break, with Mathlib's `specialUnitaryGroup` as the group.

  NOT PROVED, said exactly.
  • `ASSUMPTIONS_LEDGER` 11 stands: this file supplies the OBJECT `SU(n)` and the exponential from
    the estate's `su(n)` into it; that the physical gauge group IS this `SU(n)` (rather than another
    group with the same Lie algebra, or `U(n)`, or a quotient) is the postulate, and nothing here
    decides it.
  • Surjectivity of `exp : su(n) → SU(n)` is not proved (it needs the spectral theorem for UNITARY
    matrices, and Mathlib's is for Hermitian ones); nor is `exp` a local diffeomorphism, nor is
